// The pretty layout's two options (spec §11): `indent` and `width`, whole
// numbers of zero or more. Each case: `input` (a haus text without
// comments), the options given (an option not given is left unset, so its
// default applies), and the result of formatting `input` in the pretty
// layout: `Ok(text)`, the formatted text, or `Rejected`, a formatter that
// refuses the options (a misuse of its API, so no error code is compared).
// A binding whose API can't express an option set (a negative number in an
// unsigned type) rejects it by its types, and passes the case.

// ── options not given: the defaults (indent 2, width 80) ──
{ input: "{ a: Point(1, 2) }", result: Ok("{\n  a: Point(1, 2),\n}\n") },

